==Results==
Funes won the election with 51.3% of the vote, while Avila received 48.7%, marking the first time ARENA had lost a presidential election in 20 years.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/2/hi/americas/7944899.stm|title=Left-winger wins El Salvador poll|date=2009-03-16|work=BBC|access-date=2009-03-17}}</ref> Of the election, Funes said, "This is the happiest night of my life, and I want it to be the night of El Salvador's greatest hope. I want to thank all the people who voted for me and chose that path of hope and change."<ref name="WP">{{cite news|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-dyn/content/article/2009/03/16/AR2009031600038.html|title=Leftist Declares Victory In El Salvador Election|last=Booth|first=William|date=2009-03-16|work=Washington Post|access-date=2009-03-17}}</ref> Ávila conceded defeat, saying that he and his party "will be a constructive opposition."<ref name="WP"/> An observation team from the [[Organization of American States]] said that the elections were held without any major incidents, although there were claims of Hondurans voting at a voting center in [[Torola]], [[Morazán Department|Morazán]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://news.xinhuanet.com/english/2009-03/16/content_11017491.htm|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090318093128/http://news.xinhuanet.com/english/2009-03/16/content_11017491.htm|url-status=dead|archive-date=18 March 2009|title=OAS recognizes El Salvador's election orderly held|date=2009-03-16|work=Xinhua|access-date=2009-03-17}}</ref>

Several governments said that they looked forward to working with the new government, including [[Taiwan]] and the [[United States]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.monstersandcritics.com/news/asiapacific/news/article_1465047.php/Taiwan_to_strengthen_ties_with_El_Salvadors_next_president_|access-date=2009-03-17|title=Taiwan to strengthen ties with El Salvador's next president|date=2009-03-16|work=M&C|url-status=dead|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20090319181843/http://www.monstersandcritics.com/news/asiapacific/news/article_1465047.php/Taiwan_to_strengthen_ties_with_El_Salvadors_next_president_|archivedate=2009-03-19}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.google.com/hostednews/afp/article/ALeqM5jqH60lqIx63fXwtnwkeoWRZNMjdQ|archive-url=https://archive.today/20120731191747/http://www.google.com/hostednews/afp/article/ALeqM5jqH60lqIx63fXwtnwkeoWRZNMjdQ|url-status=dead|archive-date=31 July 2012|title=US congratulates leftist winner in El Salvador|date=2009-03-16|work=AFP|access-date=2009-03-17}}</ref>

